{
  "Name": "Adobe Flash Player copyPixelsToByteArray Method Integer Overflow",
  "Description": "This module exploits an integer overflow in Adobe Flash Player. The vulnerability occurs in the copyPixelsToByteArray method from the BitmapData object. The position field of the destination ByteArray can be used to cause an integer overflow and write contents out of the ByteArray buffer. This module has been tested successfully on: * Windows 7 SP1 (32-bit), IE 8 to IE 11 and Flash 14.0.0.176, 14.0.0.145, and 14.0.0.125. * Windows 7 SP1 (32-bit), Firefox 38.0.5 and Adobe Flash 14.0.0.179. * Windows 8.1, Firefox 38.0.5 and Adobe Flash 14.0.0.179.",
